I now have the complete picture. Here is the full trace.

## 1. The endpoint: POST /api/owners

The mapping comes from the OpenAPI-generated interface `OwnersApi` (constant `PATH_ADD_OWNER = "/owners"`, `RequestMethod.POST`), implemented by the `@RestController`:

- Controller: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`
  - Class-level `@RequestMapping("/api")` (line 54), `@RestController` (line 52), `implements OwnersApi` (line 55). So `/api` + `/owners` = `POST /api/owners`.
- Interface mapping: `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/api/OwnersApi.java` lines 79-86. The interface is annotated `@Validated` (line 44), and the body param is `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto` (line 86).

The V2 controller (`OwnerRestControllerV2.java`) only handles `GET /api/owners` paging (`listOwnersPage`), not POST.

The handler method (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, lines 100-169):

```java
100  @PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
101  @Override
102  public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
103      HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
104      Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
105      String normalizedAddress = normalizeAddress(owner.getAddress());
106      if (normalizedAddress.isEmpty()) {
107          throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST,
108              "Address must not be blank after normalization");
109      }
110      owner.setAddress(normalizedAddress);
111      String normalizedTelephone = normalizeTelephone(owner.getTelephone());
112      owner.setTelephone(normalizedTelephone);
113      owner.setEmail(normalizeEmail(owner.getEmail()));
114      java.time.LocalDate effectiveDate = owner.getRegistrationDate() != null
115          ? owner.getRegistrationDate() : java.time.LocalDate.now();
116      java.time.LocalDate businessDate = toBusinessDay(effectiveDate);
117      owner.setRegistrationDate(businessDate);
118      long createdToday = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
119          .map(Owner::getRegistrationDate)
120          .filter(businessDate::equals)
121          .count();
122      if (createdToday >= 100) {
123          throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS, ...);
124      }
125      boolean telephoneInUse = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
126          .map(Owner::getTelephone).filter(Objects::nonNull)
127          .anyMatch(normalizedTelephone::equals);
128      if (telephoneInUse) { throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT, ...); }
134      String lastNameKey = normalizeForHousehold(owner.getLastName());
135      String addressKey = normalizeForHousehold(owner.getAddress());
136      List<Owner> householdMembers = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
137          .filter(existing -> ...lastNameKey && ...addressKey).toList();
140      if (!householdMembers.isEmpty()) {
141          if (!Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold())) {
142              throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT, ...);
143          }
145          String householdId = householdId(lastNameKey, addressKey);
146          owner.setHouseholdId(householdId);
147          for (Owner member : householdMembers) {
148              if (!householdId.equals(member.getHouseholdId())) {
149                  member.setHouseholdId(householdId);
150                  this.clinicService.saveOwner(member);   // side-effect: mutates OTHER owners
151              }
152          }
153      }
154      String cityKey = normalizeForHousehold(owner.getCity());
155      long cityCount = ...count of owners in same city;
158      if (cityCount >= 50) { throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT, ...); }
162      owner.setNamesakeCount(namesakeCount(owner.getFirstName(), owner.getLastName()));
163      owner.setCustomerCode(nextCustomerCode(owner.getCity(), owner.getLastName()));
164      this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
165      OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
166      headers.setLocation(.../api/owners/{id}...buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
168      return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
169  }
```

## 2. Request DTO and its Bean Validation constraints

`@RequestBody` type is `OwnerFieldsDto`: `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/dto/OwnerFieldsDto.java`. Constraints (on the getters):

- `firstName` (line 71): `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$")`, `@Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `lastName` (line 92): `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$")`, `@Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `address` (line 113): `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(regexp = ".*\\S.*")` (must contain a non-whitespace char), `@Size(min = 1, max = 255)`
- `city` (line 134): `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(regexp = ".*\\S.*")`, `@Size(min = 1, max = 80)`
- `telephone` (line 155): `@NotNull`, `@Size(min = 1, max = 20)` — note: no `@Pattern` here (the E.164 pattern lives on the entity, see §6)
- `email` (line 176): `@Size(max = 255)`, `@Email` — optional/nullable
- `registrationDate` (line 197): `@Valid` only (no constraint); nullable
- `sharesHousehold` (line 45): no validation; defaults to `false`, not persisted

No class-level constraints. Note the request-only field `sharesHousehold` is used to bypass the household-duplicate check but is never stored on the entity.

## 3. @Valid / @Validated / custom validators / @InitBinder

- `@Valid @RequestBody` on the body param (OwnersApi.java line 86) triggers Bean Validation before the controller body runs. A failure raises `MethodArgumentNotValidException` (handled in §7) → 400, so the method body never executes.
- The interface carries `@Validated` (OwnersApi.java line 44).
- No `@InitBinder`, no `WebDataBinder` customization, and no custom `ConstraintValidator` classes exist anywhere in `src` (searched — none found). All bean-validation is stock Jakarta annotations.

## 4. Service-layer method

The controller calls `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (and `saveOwner(member)` for household members). Implementation: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`:

```java
232  @Override
233  @Transactional
234  public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
235      ownerRepository.save(owner);
236  }
```

It does no validation, normalization, or defaulting — it is a thin pass-through. `findAllOwners()` (lines 127-129, `@Transactional(readOnly = true)`) is also called repeatedly (5 separate stream scans of all owners) to implement the checks. All normalization/uniqueness/business logic lives in the controller, not the service.

The repository is profile-selected; the JPA impl `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java` (lines 93-100):

```java
public void save(Owner owner) {
    if (owner.getId() == null) { this.em.persist(owner); }
    else { this.em.merge(owner); }
}
```

## 5. Repository calls / side-effects

- `clinicService.findAllOwners()` → `ownerRepository.findAll()` — called at lines 118, 126, 136, 155, and inside `namesakeCount` (199) and `nextCustomerCode` (222): up to ~6 full-table reads per request.
- `clinicService.saveOwner(member)` (line 150) — persists changes to OTHER existing owners (back-fills their `householdId`).
- `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (line 164) → `em.persist` (insert) for the new owner.
- No `ApplicationEventPublisher`, no email sending, no audit logging anywhere (searched — none found). The only side-effects are DB writes.
- Uniqueness/business checks are all in-memory over `findAllOwners()`: telephone uniqueness (line 125), per-day cap of 100 (line 122), household duplicate by normalized lastName+address (line 140), per-city cap of 50 (line 158).

## 6. Owner entity: lifecycle callbacks, columns, constraints

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`:

- `@Entity`, `@Table(name = "owners")` — no `@UniqueConstraint`, no `@EntityListeners` (line 36-37).
- No `@PrePersist` / `@PreUpdate` callbacks, no `@CreatedDate` / auditing anywhere (searched project-wide — none found).
- Field constraints (also validated by Hibernate on flush): `address` `@NotEmpty` (line 40), `city` `@NotEmpty` (line 44), `telephone` `@NotEmpty` + `@Pattern(regexp = "^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$", ...)` (lines 48-49), `email` `@Email` (line 53). Inherited from `Person` (`/home/daniel/.../model/Person.java`): `firstName` `@NotEmpty` (line 32), `lastName` `@NotEmpty` (line 36).
- Important: the E.164 `@Pattern` on `telephone` is on the ENTITY, not the DTO — it is checked at persistence time. The controller's `normalizeTelephone` produces the `+` + 8–15 digits form so this passes. Columns without validation: `registrationDate`, `customerCode`, `householdId`, `namesakeCount`.
- `id`: from `BaseEntity` (`/home/daniel/.../model/BaseEntity.java`), `@Id @GeneratedValue(strategy = IDENTITY)`.
- DB schema `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/db/h2/schema.sql` (lines 31-45): matching NOT NULL columns on `first_name, last_name, address, city, telephone`; `email, registration_date, customer_code, household_id, namesake_count` nullable. There is NO UNIQUE constraint on telephone (or any owner column) at the DB level — telephone uniqueness is enforced ONLY by the in-memory controller check at line 125.

## 7. Global exception handling for this path

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java` (`@ControllerAdvice`, line 50):

- `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400 (lines 153-190). Builds a `ProblemDetail`, sets `errors` (distinct invalid field names) and `schemaValidationErrors` (per-field messages incl. rejected value). This is what Bean Validation failures on the DTO map to.
- `ResponseStatusException` → passes the status/reason through (lines 99-107). This is what every business-rule `throw` in `addOwner` uses: 400 (blank address / bad telephone), 429 (daily cap), 409 (telephone dup / household dup / city cap).
- `DataIntegrityViolationException` → 404 (lines 133-144) — note it maps DB constraint violations to 404, not 409.
- `AccessDeniedException` → re-thrown for Spring Security to yield 403 (lines 85-88).
- `Exception` (catch-all) → 500 (lines 116-123).

## 8. @Transactional annotations

- `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` — `@Transactional` (write) (line 233).
- `ClinicServiceImpl.findAllOwners` — `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` (line 126).
- The controller method `addOwner` is NOT `@Transactional`. Consequently each `saveOwner`/`findAllOwners` call runs in its own separate transaction. The multiple household-member saves (line 150) and the final owner save (line 164) are therefore NOT atomic with one another, and the uniqueness reads are not in the same transaction as the write (a TOCTOU race window exists). (The V1 `deleteOwner` at line 376 has `@Transactional`, but `addOwner` does not.)

## Order of operations for a successful create

1. Argument resolution: Jackson deserializes body → `OwnerFieldsDto`; `@Valid` runs Bean Validation on the DTO (firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone/email). Failure → 400 via `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, body never runs.
2. `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)")` security check; failure → 403.
3. `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` — maps fields; ignores `id` and `pets` (OwnerMapper line 35-37).
4. `normalizeAddress` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE); if empty → 400.
5. Set normalized address.
6. `normalizeTelephone` (strip non-digits, apply +61 default / keep country code, validate 8–15 digits); invalid → 400.
7. Set normalized telephone.
8. `normalizeEmail` (lower-case, null-safe) and set.
9. Compute effective registration date (supplied or `now()`), roll to business day via `toBusinessDay` (Sat→+2, Sun→+1), set it.
10. Daily cap: count owners whose registrationDate equals this business day; ≥100 → 429.
11. Telephone uniqueness: scan all owners; match → 409.
12. Household dup: compute normalized lastName+address keys; if matching owners exist and `sharesHousehold != true` → 409; otherwise compute SHA-256-based `householdId`, set it on the new owner, and back-fill/save that householdId onto existing members (writes to other rows).
13. City cap: count owners in same normalized city; ≥50 → 409.
14. Set `namesakeCount` (count of pre-existing same first+last name, case-insensitive).
15. Set `customerCode` (`CITY3-LAST3-NNNN`, per-city sequence).
16. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` → `em.persist` (insert); Hibernate re-validates entity constraints incl. telephone E.164 `@Pattern` on flush.
17. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` (derives displayName, initials, membershipNumber, membershipTier, locality).
18. Set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return 201 CREATED.

